+### REQ-VERIFY-5541: LLM-FSM Deterministic Exact Fixture V502
+
+The repository SHALL provide Exp 5541 at
+`python/carnot/experiment_5541_llm_fsm_exact_fixture.py` and write
+`results/experiment_5541_llm_fsm_exact_fixture.json` as a deterministic
+finite-state exact benchmark substrate inspired by the V502 LLM-FSM literature
+refresh. Exp 5541 SHALL define a compact configurable FSM family with explicit
+state count, transition sparsity, accepting states, error states, transition
+constraints, and observable traces. The workflow SHALL emit schema-valid
+machine descriptions plus deterministic natural-language summaries, and SHALL
+derive every reference trace label from the machine definition rather than from
+an LLM or hand-labeled prose.
+
+The exact checker SHALL cover trace acceptance, transition consistency,
+unreachable-state detection, contradiction detection, and brute-force finite
+SAT-style completion checks for the bounded fixtures. The fixture family SHALL
+include at least one satisfiable instance, one unsatisfiable instance, and one
+ambiguous or underconstrained instance. The ambiguous instance SHALL keep
+underconstrained traces visible instead of promoting them to accepted or
+rejected labels. Exp 5541 SHALL NOT invoke an LLM, SHALL NOT load a model, and
+SHALL NOT modify `scripts/research_conductor.py`.
+
+The artifact SHALL include at minimum these top-level fields:
+`fsm_instances`, `state_counts`, `transition_constraints`,
+`satisfiable_instances`, `unsatisfiable_instances`, `ambiguous_instances`,
+`yaml_schema_valid`, `reference_trace_checks_passed`,
+`exact_transition_checks_passed`, `sat_solver_checks_passed`,
+`no_llm_invoked`, `exact_fsm_fixture_ready`, `tests_added_or_reused`,
+`field_principles`, `inference_substrate`, and `honest_verdict`.
+`inference_substrate` SHALL equal
+`deterministic_fsm_exact_fixture_no_llm`; `no_llm_invoked` SHALL be `true`; and
+`honest_verdict` SHALL start with `complete:` or `blocked:`.
+
+Field principles:
+
+- `fsm_instances`: Fixes the number of generated FSM rows so later panels keep
+  the denominator visible.
+- `state_counts`: Records fixture scale without relying on prose summaries.
+- `transition_constraints`: Makes the exact transition substrate inspectable.
+- `satisfiable_instances`: Counts clean exact machines separately from nulls.
+- `unsatisfiable_instances`: Preserves contradiction controls as first-class
+  evidence.
+- `ambiguous_instances`: Preserves underconstrained controls without forcing a
+  false label.
+- `yaml_schema_valid`: Confirms emitted machine descriptions are parseable and
+  schema-shaped.
+- `reference_trace_checks_passed`: Confirms trace labels are generated by exact
+  execution or completion analysis.
+- `exact_transition_checks_passed`: Confirms transition consistency and
+  contradiction checks agree with fixture intent.
+- `sat_solver_checks_passed`: Confirms bounded completion enumeration agrees
+  with the expected satisfiable, unsatisfiable, and ambiguous classes.
+- `no_llm_invoked`: Prevents this exact fixture from being mistaken for a live
+  model result.
+- `exact_fsm_fixture_ready`: Opens only when schema, trace, transition, and
+  SAT-style gates all pass.
+- `tests_added_or_reused`: Links the artifact to tests that exercise the exact
+  checker.
+- `field_principles`: Explains why every headline and gate field exists.
+- `inference_substrate`: Declares deterministic FSM enumeration as the evidence
+  substrate.
+- `honest_verdict`: Provides a terminal evidence boundary without a model
+  quality claim.
+
+### SCENARIO-VERIFY-5541: Exact FSM Fixture Separates Sat, Unsat, And Ambiguous Rows
+
+Given the compact FSM family configuration, when Exp 5541 runs, then it builds
+schema-valid machine descriptions, derives deterministic trace labels by exact
+finite execution or completion enumeration, reports unreachable states,
+detects transition contradictions, enumerates bounded deterministic
+completions, writes `results/experiment_5541_llm_fsm_exact_fixture.json`, and
+sets `exact_fsm_fixture_ready=true` only when satisfiable, unsatisfiable, and
+ambiguous controls are all present and all exact checks pass.
+
+If a required transition conflicts with another required transition, if a
+required transition is also forbidden, if a state reference is invalid, if no
+completion exists, or if multiple completions produce different trace labels,
+then Exp 5541 SHALL record the contradiction or underconstrained status
+directly, SHALL keep `reference_trace_checks_passed` and
+`sat_solver_checks_passed` false unless the observed exact class matches the
+fixture intent, and SHALL keep `no_llm_invoked=true` regardless of outcome.
+
